  "description": "Surendra Singh Pangtey introduces himself in Johari, a dialect of Kumaoni. Pangtey is an author and a former Indian Army and Indian Administrative Service officer. He speaks two main forms of Johari. One was used mostly in the past in very particular settings, such as when two Shauka riders greet each other as their horses pass. It uses many words from Rankas and Shaukiya-Khun, older forms that are no longer spoken. The other, known as Johari, is what the Shauka people use in everyday conversation. This video is from Johari (जोहारी), a 2026 short film by Subhashish Panigrahi in OpenSpeaks Archives, made from footage recorded for his 2021 documentary MarginalizedAadhaar. Subtitles are by Pangtey, edited by Panigrahi.",
